{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sn4otkxr54rz67vwkzxfuirloowaszh5efiqursir5lh343wsxrq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Verification complete — all four gates pass\n\n**What the project actually is:** `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` is `add_executable` only — a single 33-line translation unit whose only function is `main`. So I built the C side as a `.so` by renaming `main` on the *compiler command line* (`gcc -shared -fPIC -Dmain=driver_main`, nothing in `c_src/` touched), restructured the Rust into `lib.rs` (`rlib` + `cdylib`, `#[no_mangle] driver_main`) + a 3-line `main.rs` shim, and drove **both** `.so`s through `libloading` from a re-exec'd runner child, plus both executables at the process boundary.\n\n### Bugs found and fixed in the Rust (5 real divergence classes)\n\n| # | Divergence | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `print!` **panicked** on a failed stdout write (EPIPE/ENOSPC/EBADF); C ignores the error and still `return 0`s | `write_all` with the `Result` discarded |\n| 2 | Rust's runtime forces `SIGPIPE=SIG_IGN` before `main`, so a broken pipe aborted (SIGABRT 6) instead of killing with **SIGPIPE 13** | capture the inherited disposition from an ELF `.init_array` constructor (runs before `lang_start`) and restore it |\n| 3 | `raise(SIGFPE)` is *not* equivalent to a hardware `#DE`: it silently returns when SIGFPE is ignored or blocked | emit the real `cdq; idiv` via `core::arch::asm!` — byte-identical to what glibc's `div` compiles to (verified by `objdump`) |\n| 4 | `io::stdin()`'s 8 KiB `BufReader` **over-consumed** shared stdin (C uses `st_blksize`=4096) | read blocks straight off fd 0, sized like `_IO_file_doallocate` |\n| 5 | Rust never performed glibc's exit-time `lseek` rewind, so `{ ./driver; cat; } < f` printed *nothing* where C printed the tail | replicate `_IO_new_file_sync` after the stdout flush (and *not* on the signal path) |\n\n### Anti-vacuity: 11 mutations injected, 11 caught\nIncluding one that exposed a **real harness bug**: `cargo test` never builds the `cdylib`, so removing `#[no_mangle]` still \"passed\" against a stale `.so`. The harness now refreshes the cdylib itself and refuses to run against artifacts older than their source.\n\n### Final gate\n```\nGATE 1  nm -D diff .................. EMPTY   (C={driver_main} Rust={driver_main}), 0 unresolved imports\nGATE 2  CONFIGS.md rows ............. 29/29 pass across randomized inputs (seed 20260818)\nGATE 3  ERRORS.md rows .............. 32/32 pass; 0 unchecked boxes; 0 stubs/unimplemented!\nGATE 4  configurations .............. 6/6  (no-default-features | all-features | default) × (dev | release)\n        62 rows × 6185 cases per config, 0 [FAIL], SCRIPT_EXIT=0\n```\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/differential.rs` (2542 lines), `check_all_configs.sh`, `logs/verification-matrix.log`.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: the `idiv` inline-asm path and the 4096-byte block size are **x86-64/glibc-specific** (I added `cfg` fallbacks for aarch64 and other ISAs, but those are untested here since aarch64's `sdiv` doesn't trap at all — a genuine behavioral difference in the *C* on that platform). Also, `E30`'s \"out-of-range enum across FFI\" row has no literal enum to corrupt, so I tested the nearest real thing: calling `driver_main` through a mis-declared six-integer-argument fn pointer full of garbage."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":887,"cache_read_input_tokens":243141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":887,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d7bdec0-464b-4778-924d-8903d98dcab0","uuid":"44e29b83-0651-4e5f-9a79-bf2677b8a6f6","timestamp":"2026-08-18T05:07:08.024Z"}
